---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../lib/site';
import { ROWS, AUTHORITIES } from '../../data/complianceMap';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tools"
  description="Free working tools built from the Corrections Pest Reference: a facility compliance map and printable checklist, a pest grievance worksheet and log, a model pest control policy, and a model pest management scope of work for correctional facility contracts."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Tools', url: `${SITE_URL}/tools/` }]}
>
  <style>
    .tool { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: 1.25rem 0; }
    .tool h2 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
    .tool h2 a { color: var(--color-primary); }
    .tool p { margin: 0.3rem 0; max-width: 46rem; }
  </style>

  <h1>Tools</h1>
  <p>Built from the same primary sources as the authority pages. Free to use.</p>

  <div class="tool">
    <h2><a href="/tools/compliance-map/">Pest Compliance Map</a></h2>
    <p>
      {ROWS.length} requirements from {AUTHORITIES.length} authorities, federal and in 30 states, each paired with the record that shows it
      was met, how often, and who the text names as responsible. Set a facility profile to keep only what applies. Print it as an
      inspection checklist, download a ready-made PDF for each state's county jails, or export the filtered map as a spreadsheet.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="tool">
    <h2><a href="/tools/vermin-grievance-file/">The Vermin Grievance File</a></h2>
    <p>
      The eight questions plaintiff's counsel asks about a pest grievance, each paired with the record that answers it. A printable
      worksheet built on the deliberate-indifference test in Farmer v. Brennan and Antonelli v. Sheahan.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="tool">
    <h2><a href="/tools/grievance-loop/">Grievance-to-Work-Order Loop</a></h2>
    <p>
      A one-page log that ties each pest grievance to its work order, response, follow-up check, and answer, with the five places
      the loop usually breaks. Prints landscape.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="tool">
    <h2><a href="/tools/pest-control-policy/">Model Pest Control Policy</a></h2>
    <p>
      The written policy many standards ask for, filled in for your state: responsibility, licensed service at a set frequency,
      pest reports closed as work orders, food service, infested persons and property, pesticide storage, records, and review.
      For agencies on Lexipol's custody manual, a way to review Policy 805. Word download for each state.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tool">
    <h2><a href="/tools/scope-of-work/">Model Scope of Work</a></h2>
    <p>
      Contract language for a correctional facility pest management solicitation or renewal: qualifications, frequency, device
      map, application records, written findings, pesticide management, exclusion, and buyer-protective terms, filled in for your
      state. Word download for each state.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>Working with member jails as a risk pool or insurer? See <a href="/risk-pools/">For Risk Pools</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
